{
 "acceptance": "Facet acceptance rules, one rule set for both encoders of both implementations (the permissive symbol() and the checked encoders apply it alike) and for both preflight tools. numeric: integers within (-2^53, 2^53), integral floats, booleans as 0 and 1; fractional numbers, every string, and non scalar values are refused; null is missing. boolean: booleans, and numbers exactly 0 or 1; anything else is refused; null is missing. categorical: strings only; null is missing. Every conversion that remains is one the engine cannot tell apart, so an accepted value decides as the raw value does.",
 "changes": "Version 2 (October 2026, step 3 of the reading boundary plan): a string on a numeric field is refused as wrong_type rather than parsed, because the engine never orders a string against a number, so accepting \"5\" as 5 routed it where the engine would not. Each case or reading whose expectation changed carries `changed.was`, its version 1 expectation. Parsing belongs to the adapter.",
 "version": 2,
